Original commit body from 9d236307b13b0dca44b250de1d4be6cd3dd428fc:

A variable's type now belongs to the function that binds it. A type written for a same-named variable in another function of the file no longer types it. Ten languages: Java, Kotlin, JavaScript, TypeScript, C#, Groovy, Scala, Rust, Ruby, Lua. Addresses INV-zabud (owner ruling 2026-11-24; the owner saw the counts below before the merge and ruled "merge as built").

WHAT WAS WRONG
One variable-type dict per file, kept in one of two ways. Filled during the edge walk (JavaScript, TypeScript, Scala, C#, Groovy; Java and Kotlin for parameters): a later function's untyped `db` kept the type the previous function gave its own `db`. Filled by a walk of its own, first writer wins (Rust, Ruby, Lua): the first `db` in the file typed every `db`, one constructed on the line above its call included.

WHAT CHANGED
- hypergumbo_core/analyze/var_scope.py, ScopedVarTypes: the same dict, whose bindings close with their function. One class, ten users. Java and Kotlin each had a hand-written copy of the mechanism for locals; both are deleted.
- JavaScript / TypeScript: `this.<name>` receivers read a table filled from constructor parameters only.
- ADR-0006: the Scope Handling section, the table's Scope column, limitation 1 and future-work 9.
- One commit per language.

SCOREBOARD
Fixture (one program, 17 languages), the two new columns before -> after:
- scope_own (a function constructs its own `h`, another function binds an `h` of the decoy class): lua, ruby, rust `order:right/decoy` -> `right`.
- scope_ext (`h` comes from outside the repository): java, kotlin `order:unresolved/picked` -> `unresolved`; javascript, typescript, lua, rust, scala `picked` -> `unresolved`; ruby `picked` -> `no_edge`. csharp and groovy read `picked` before and after: they also bind an untyped receiver by name alone (WI-dovoz, WI-tiluh); test_var_types_per_function.py asks them directly.
- ruby amb_param `no_edge` -> `unresolved`.

